            "paragraph": "Climate in the Euro-Atlantic region is strongly shaped by the North Atlantic large-scale atmospheric cir- culation 1-3. Of central importance is the eddy-driven jet stream (hereafter jet), a band of strong westerly winds extending across the North Atlantic basin. The jet steers North Atlantic extratropical cyclones and, through this, plays a central role in shaping European weather and climate 4,5. The jet dynamics are closely linked to large-scale modes of variability, such as the North Atlantic Oscillation (NAO) 6-8, along with key dynamical processes including Rossby wave breaking 9,10 and impactful phenomena like atmospheric blocking 11,12.",
